// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6218 Add Git configuration command execution rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6218
// Pull request author: signalblur
// Change: new rule
// Title: Git Pack or Proxy Program Override - Windows
// Sigma ID: c2aa5eed-954c-4b1a-9e52-2ebb0afcf4d8
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: David Burkett (@signalblur)
// Date: 2026-08-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects Git being told to run a caller-supplied program in place of one of the helpers it
//   normally starts for itself. The "--upload-pack" and "--receive-pack" options, their
//   "remote.<name>.uploadpack" and "remote.<name>.receivepack" configuration equivalents,
//   "uploadpack.packObjectsHook" and "core.gitProxy" each name a program that Git executes while
//   moving objects to or from a repository. Against a local path or a local clone that program runs
//   on the host issuing the command, which turns an otherwise ordinary looking Git invocation into
//   command execution.
// False positives:
//   - Connecting to a server that keeps Git outside the default path, which is the documented reason to pass "--upload-pack" or "--receive-pack".
//   - A proxy program configured for the deprecated "git://" protocol in an environment that still restricts direct outbound connections.
// References:
//   - https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config
//   - https://git-scm.com/docs/git-clone
//   - https://git-scm.com/docs/git-push
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/525309ab68cce53dd9b31a4b81cd80862b6058f6/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_git_pack_proxy_program_override.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\git.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--receive-pack" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--upload-pack" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".receivepack" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".uploadpack" or ProcessCommandLine contains "core.gitProxy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "uploadpack.packObjectsHook")
